{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Your fullness.</b> An obligation laid upon you when your produce fills for ripening — and that is first fruits." "<b>And your tears.</b> The terumah — and I do not know what the term דֶּמַע means." "<b>You shall not delay.</b> You shall not change the order of their separation, delaying what is earlier and advancing what is later — that one should not advance terumah before first fruits or tithe before terumah (Mekhilta)." "<b>Your firstborn son you shall give Me.</b> To redeem him with five selas to the priest. But has He not already commanded him on this elsewhere? Rather, in order to place next to it ״כֵּן תַּעֲשֶׂה לְשֹׁרְךָ״ — just as a human firstborn, after thirty days, one redeems him, as stated ״וּפְדוּיָו מִבֶּן חֹדֶשׁ תִּפְדֶּה״ (Numbers 18), so too a firstborn of small animals one tends it thirty days and afterwards gives it to the priest (Bekhorot 26)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:01.652684634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}